## 4. No-direct-equivalent cases

| surface | linux construct | why no win32 equivalent | redesign |
|---------|-----------------|--------------------------|----------|
| chs_rt_landlock.c:79,156,191,211,207 | syscall __NR_landlock_* + prctl(PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS) | Linux-only LSM; no syscall on Win32; no `no_new_privs` flag. | Windows Job Object + restricted token + NTFS DACL on the allowlist. Map `oo_landlock_restrict` to a new `&WindowsCap` that builds a Job Object and assigns it to the current process. Refuse where Landlock would refuse. |
| chs_rt_rlimit.c:31 (RLIMIT_NOFILE) | setrlimit(RLIMIT_NOFILE, ...) | Win32 has no per-process fd cap (handles scale with kernel pool). | Degrade to ignore: return `OK` with a stderr note. The shim warns the user and does not change fd count. |
| chs_rt_rlimit.c:45 (RLIMIT_CPU soft) | setrlimit(RLIMIT_CPU, &rl) | Win32 has no CPU-second soft/hard split; Job Object CPU is a rate, not seconds. | Use Job Object `JOB_OBJECT_CPU_RATE_CONTROL` (percent). Convert "seconds" -> "percent of one core" in the shim. |
| chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:115-119 (/dev/null) | open("/dev/null", O_RDWR) + dup2 | Path-only convention `NUL` is reserved but not the same fd. | CreateFileA("NUL", GENERIC_READ\|GENERIC_WRITE) + SetStdHandle(STD_INPUT_HANDLE/...). |
| chs_rt_ffi_sec.c:123 (execlp minisign) | execlp("minisign", ...) | execlp PATH search has no Win32 equivalent. | CreateProcessA: search PATH in shim, pass full path. |
| chs_rt_sys.c:158 (/proc/self/cmdline) | fopen("/proc/self/cmdline","rb") | /proc is Linux-only. | GetCommandLineA and CommandLineToArgvW. |
| chs_rt_hitl.c:42 (/dev/tty) | fopen("/dev/tty","r") | /dev/tty is Linux/BSD. | CreateFileA("CONIN$", ...). |
| chs_rt_libfloor.c:129,137 (epoll/inotify) | oo_sys_epoll_create / oo_sys_inotify_init (already residual Err) | Already sealed behind SysCap as Err; no product claim. | Keep the shim: same residual Err on Windows. |
| chs_rt_libfloor.c:144 (prctl) | oo_sys_prctl (already residual Err) | No Win32 equivalent for the Linux prctl namespace. | Keep the shim: same residual Err on Windows. |
| chs_rt_sys.c:46 (clearenv) | clearenv / environ rewrite | Win32 has no envp pointer block; env is per-process query. | Walk `GetEnvironmentStrings`, rebuild via SetEnvironmentVariable. |
| chs_rt_xlang.c:80 (system gcc) | system("gcc -flto ...") | system is CRT; "gcc" must be "gcc.exe" on Windows. | Detect host, emit "gcc.exe" form; PATH already required. |

## 5. Summary counts

- POSIX-only or Linux-only call sites in ooda/runtime: 95.
- Direct Windows equivalent (CreateFile / LoadLibrary / Winsock / BCryptGenRandom / CRITICAL_SECTION / CloseHandle / GetFileAttributesEx / etc.): 86.
- No direct equivalent (redesign needed): 9 (the 9 rows of section 4; epoll/inotify/prctl are residual Err and only count once each).
- Public-path rows: 88. Internal-only rows: 18.
- Landlock and RLIMIT_NOFILE are the only two POSIX-isms the SHIPPED.oot currently exercises as a product path; the master plan already names them. setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS/RLIMIT_CPU) get Job Object wrappers; the fd cap degrades to a no-op with a stderr note.
- pthread_cond_wait / pthread_cond_timedwait / pthread_cond_broadcast are NOT used. Channels (chs_rt_channel.c) are non-blocking by design (line 6-7 comment). Only `pthread_cond_init` and `pthread_cond_signal` are present. Windows CONDITION_VARIABLE has direct equivalents.

## 6. What was not checked

- chs_rt_host.c full call graph under OODA_WITH_HOST_FFI. The shim is the host staticlib, not the runtime; oodac is the host. The runtime only declares `extern char *ooda_host_*` and calls them. Not in this audit's POSIX-call scope.
- oo_holo.c: only C stdio (fopen/fread/fwrite) confirmed. File size 144 lines, not fully re-read. Low risk (no POSIX-only headers).
- oo_sha256.c: not opened. Filename suggests NIST SHA only. Low risk.
- chs_rt_str_ops.c, chs_rt_str_int.c, chs_rt_str_tok.c, chs_rt_str_intern.c, chs_rt_str.c, chs_rt_hash.c, chs_rt_math.c, chs_rt_emit_tmp.c, chs_rt_list_set.c, chs_rt_wasm.c, chs_rt_wasm_print.c: grepped; no POSIX-only headers found. Internal-only stdlib + abort/exit (CRT). Read once to confirm.
- Setjmp / longjmp / sigaction / sigprocmask: not found in any chs_rt_*.c.
- memfd_create / seccomp / eventfd / timerfd / signalfd / mmap / mprotect / msync / getrandom: not found in any chs_rt_*.c. epoll/inotify/prctl exist only as residual Err stubs in chs_rt_libfloor.c.
- The C stdlib (stdio.h, stdlib.h, string.h, time.h) is portable; this audit did not flag it.
- The audit is read-only. No edits to ooda/runtime/, no mingw build, no .oo generation.
